  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Applications of Composition - Ripple Area</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A stone is dropped into a pond, creating a circular ripple. If the radius of the ripple increases at a rate of {@dr@} cm/s, express the area of the ripple as a function of time.</p>

<p>\(A(t):\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<p>The area of a circle is:</p>
<p>\[
A(r) = \pi r^2
\]</p>

<p>The radius as a function of time is:</p>
<p>\[
r(t) = {@dr@} t \quad (\text{starting from } r = 0)
\]</p>

<p>The area as a function of time is the composition:</p>
<p>\[
A(t) = (A \circ r)(t) = A(r(t)) = A({@dr@} t)
= \pi ({@dr@} t)^2
= {@dr^2@}\pi t^2.
\]</p>]]></text>
