<!-- question: 169558 -->
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Applications of Composition - Sand Pile Volume</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Sand is being poured onto a conical pile. The height of the pile is always {@k@} times the radius of the base. If the height increases at a rate of {@dh@} cm/s, express the volume of the pile as a function of time.</p>

<p>\(V(t):\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<p>The volume of a cone is:</p>
<p>\[
V = \frac{1}{3} \pi r^2 h
\]</p>

<p>We are given that \(h = {@k@} r\), so \(r = \frac{h}{ {@k@} }\).</p>
<p>Substituting \(r\) into the volume formula:</p>
<p>\[
V(h) = \frac{1}{3} \pi \left(\frac{h}{ {@k@} }\right)^2 h = \frac{\pi h^3}{3 \cdot {@k^2@}}
\]</p>

<p>The height as a function of time is:</p>
<p>\[
h(t) = {@dh@} t \quad (\text{starting from } h = 0)
\]</p>

<p>The volume as a function of time is:</p>
<p>\[
V(t) = V(h(t)) = \frac{\pi ({@dh@} t)^3}{3 \cdot {@k^2@}}
= \frac{\pi \cdot {@dh^3@} t^3}{ {@3*k^2@} }.
\]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
