  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Applications of Composition - Sphere Surface Area</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A spherical balloon is being inflated. If the radius increases at a rate of {@dr@} cm/s, express the surface area as a function of time.</p>

<p>\(S(t):\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<p>The surface area of a sphere is:</p>
<p>\[
S(r) = 4 \pi r^2
\]</p>

<p>The radius as a function of time is:</p>
<p>\[
r(t) = {@dr@} t \quad (\text{starting from } r = 0)
\]</p>

<p>The surface area as a function of time is the composition:</p>
<p>\[
S(t) = (S \circ r)(t) = S(r(t)) = S({@dr@} t)
= 4 \pi ({@dr@} t)^2
= 4 \pi \cdot {@dr^2@} t^2
= {@4*dr^2@} \pi t^2.
\]</p>]]></text>
